Ours.  Declarations gcc 14 needs in the font libraries (lib/font, FSlib):
each file that called a function with no declaration gets a prototype after its
includes, taken from the definition the call links with (gcc -aux-info).  A K&R
definition's narrow parameters are default-promoted in the prototype, as a K&R caller
passes them (char/short/their typedefs -> int, float -> double):
  lib/font/Type1/scanfont.c: objFormatReal(float value -> double); objFormatBoolean(boolean value -> int)
  lib/font/bitmap/bdfread.c: bdfSpecialProperty(char isString -> int)
Declared without a prototype (types not defined at that point, or called with varying
arguments; none has an ANSI definition with a narrow parameter): client_auth_generation 
ClientSignal _FontTransClose _FSDisconnectServer _FSTransGetConnectionNumber 
init_fs_handlers remove_fs_handlers Type1OpenScalable XpClientIsBitmapClient 
XpClientIsPrintClient 
Headers whose macros call a function get a declaration beside the macro: 
lib/font/include/fntfilio.h lib/font/include/fontmisc.h lib/font/Speedo/spdo_prv.h 
lib/font/Type1/objects.h lib/font/Type1/t1stdio.h lib/FS/FSlibint.h 

